<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000092> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                            rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000052> ;
                                            rdfs:comment "This relation is modeled after the BFO relation of the same name which was in BFO2, but is used in a more restricted sense - specifically, we model this relation as functional (inherited from characteristic-of). Note that this relation is now removed from BFO2020." ;
                                            rdfs:label "disposition of"@en .


###  http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0001015
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0001015> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                            rdfs:subPropertyOf tara:roObjectProperty ;
                                            owl:inverseOf <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0001025> ;
                                            rdf:type owl:TransitiveProperty ;
                                            <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000111> "is location of"@en ;
                                            <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112> "my head is the location of my brain"@en ,
                                                                                         "this cage is the location of this rat"@en ;
                                            <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "a relation between two independent continuants, the location and the target, in which the target is entirely within the location"@en ;
                                            <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Most location relations will only hold at certain times, but this is difficult to specify in OWL. See http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ro/docs/temporal-semantics/"@en ;
                                            rdfs:label "location of"@en .


###  http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0001025
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0001025> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                            rdfs:subPropertyOf tara:roObjectProperty ;
                                            rdf:type owl:TransitiveProperty ;
                                            rdfs:domain <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000004> ,
                                                        [ owl:intersectionOf ( <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000004>
                                                                               [ rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                                                 owl:complementOf <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000006>
                                                                               ]
                                                                             ) ;
                                                          rdf:type owl:Class
                                                        ] ;
                                            rdfs:range <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000004> ,
                                                       [ owl:intersectionOf ( <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000004>
                                                                              [ rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                                                owl:complementOf <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000006>
                                                                              ]
                                                                            ) ;
                                                         rdf:type owl:Class
                                                       ] ;
                                            owl:propertyChainAxiom ( <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0001025>
                                                                     <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050>
                                                                   ) ;
                                            <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000111> "located in"@en ;
                                            <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112> "my brain is located in my head"@en ,
                                                                                         "this rat is located in this cage"@en ;
                                            <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "c is located_in c1 (at a time t) if and only if the spatial region occupied by c is part_of the spatial region occupied by c1 (at t). This relation comprehends both exact location (as when a portion of fluid exactly fills a cavity) and inexact/containment-style location (as between brain and head, or ovum and uterus)." ;
                                            <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "Chosen over overlaps (RO:0002131) for the Acupoint surface-anatomy and meridian relations because located_in does not require the two related continuants to be of the same BFO category (material vs. immaterial), unlike overlaps, which requires a literal shared part. The property-chain axiom (located_in o part_of -> located_in) means that if c is located_in c1 and c1 is part_of c2, then c is automatically inferred located_in c2 as well." ,
                                                                                         "Location as a relation between instances: The primitive instance-level relation c located_in r at t reflects the fact that each continuant is at any given time associated with exactly one spatial region, namely its exact location. Following we can use this relation to define a further instance-level location relation - not between a continuant and the region which it exactly occupies, but rather between one continuant and another. c is located in c1, in this sense, whenever the spatial region occupied by c is part_of the spatial region occupied by c1.    Note that this relation comprehends both the relation of exact location between one continuant and another which obtains when r and r1 are identical (for example, when a portion of fluid exactly fills a cavity), as well as those sorts of inexact location relations which obtain, for example, between brain and head or between ovum and uterus"@en ,
                                                                                         "Most location relations will only hold at certain times, but this is difficult to specify in OWL. See http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ro/docs/temporal-semantics/"@en ;
                                            <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000118> "located_in"@en ;
                                            <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "OBO Relations Ontology (RO), http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ro.owl." ;
                                            <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000412> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ro.owl> ;
                                            dcterms:source "http://www.obofoundry.org/ro/#OBO_REL:located_in" ;
                                            rdfs:label "located in"@en .

[ rdf:type owl:Axiom ;
   owl:annotatedSource <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0001025> ;
   owl:annotatedProperty rdfs:range ;
   owl:annotatedTarget <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000004> ;
   <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "This is redundant with the more specific 'independent and not spatial region' constraint. We leave in the redundant axiom for use with reasoners that do not use negation."
 ] .

[ rdf:type owl:Axiom ;
   owl:annotatedSource <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0001025> ;
   owl:annotatedProperty rdfs:domain ;
   owl:annotatedTarget <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000004> ;
   <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "This is redundant with the more specific 'independent and not spatial region' constraint. We leave in the redundant axiom for use with reasoners that do not use negation."
 ] .


###  http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002131
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002131> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                            rdfs:subPropertyOf tara:roObjectProperty ;
                                            rdf:type owl:SymmetricProperty ;
                                            <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112> "LU1 hasRelatedSubSurfaceAnatomy Axillary Artery." ;
                                            <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "x overlaps y if and only if there exists some z such that x has part z and z part of y." ;
                                            <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> "part_of (BFO:0000050) is itself a subproperty of overlaps in RO's own hierarchy (is_a: RO:0002131 overlaps), since anything that is part_of something automatically overlaps it -- this is why overlaps, not part_of, is the true root of this branch." ;
                                            <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "OBO Relations Ontology (RO), http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ro.owl." ;
                                            <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000412> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ro.owl> ;
                                            rdfs:label "overlaps" .


###  http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002170
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002170> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                            rdfs:subPropertyOf tara:roObjectProperty ;
                                            owl:inverseOf <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002176> ;
                                            <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112> "a 'toe distal phalanx bone' that is connected to a 'toe medial phalanx bone' (an interphalangeal joint *connects* these two bones)." ;
                                            <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "a is connected to b if and only if a and b are discrete structure, and there exists some connecting structure c, such that c connects a and b."@en ;
                                            <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000412> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ro.owl> ;
                                            rdfs:label "connected to"@en .


###  http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002176
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002176> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                            rdfs:subPropertyOf tara:roObjectProperty ;
                                            <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "c connects a if and only if there exist some b such that a and b are similar parts of the same system, and c connects b, specifically, c connects a with b. When one structure connects two others it unites some aspect of the function or role they play within the system."@en ;
                                            <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000412> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ro.owl> ;
                                            rdfs:label "connects"@en .


###  http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002350
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002350> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                            rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000050> ;
                                            owl:inverseOf <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002351> ;
                                            <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000112> "An organism that is a member of a population of organisms" ;
                                            <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "is member of is a mereological relation between a item and a collection." ;
                                            <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000118> "is member of" ,
                                                                                         "member part of" ;
                                            <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "SIO" ;
                                            rdfs:label "member of"@en .


###  http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002351
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002351> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                            rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000051> ;
                                            rdf:type owl:IrreflexiveProperty ;
                                            <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "has member is a mereological relation between a collection and an item." ;
                                            <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000119> "SIO" ;
                                            rdfs:label "has member"@en .


###  http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0004026
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0004026> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                            rdfs:subPropertyOf tara:roObjectProperty ;
                                            <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "A relationship between a disease and an anatomical entity where the disease has one or more features that are located in that entity."@en ;
                                            <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000412> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ro.owl> ;
                                            rdfs:label "disease has location"@en .


###  http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0004027
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0004027> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                            rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0004026> ;
                                            <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "A relationship between a disease and an anatomical entity where the disease is triggered by an inflammatory response to stimuli occurring in the anatomical entity."@en ;
                                            <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000412> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ro.owl> ;
                                            rdfs:label "disease has inflammation site"@en .


###  http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0004029
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0004029> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                            rdfs:subPropertyOf tara:roObjectProperty ;
                                            <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> "A relationship between a disease and some feature of that disease, where the feature is either a phenotype or an isolated disease."@en ;
                                            <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000412> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ro.owl> ;
                                            rdfs:label "disease has feature"@en .


###  http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/mondo#disease_has_major_feature
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/mondo#disease_has_major_feature> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                                 rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0004029> .


